{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ef48e947a4c70e998653430bb13a9d08a072ac9319e2842cade50995f0f1d32c","digest":{"component_or_area":"repo-isolation test infrastructure","key_entities":["tests/_isolation.py","tests/conftest.py","porcelain()","head()","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_commits","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","_run_process"],"problem_keywords":["subprocess timeout","git probe","unbounded blocking","test teardown","repo isolation","pytest hook","liveness"],"propositions":["Git status and HEAD probes in repo-isolation hooks run without a subprocess timeout, potentially keeping pytest alive indefinitely if a probe blocks.","The five-second timeout watchdog on both porcelain() and head() must explicitly raise subprocess.TimeoutExpired rather than silently returning None.","Test monkeypatches of subprocess.run and time.sleep can contaminate autuse teardown; real process and sleep primitives must be captured at module import.","Both read-only Git probes must be exercised through their real hook callers (pytest_sessionfinish and _no_repo_commits) with deterministic blocking Git shims."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787411627457411001,"uuid":"994a4a68-ff9b-4fe9-851c-30910aa06fc0"}